Z||000006||batboy||03-25-2001||01:15 PM||||Since I'm soooo lazy lately, was hoping someone else would get off their butt and measure this for you, since that ain't happening, here you go. Measurements are the inside box opening dimensions not including the outer mounting lip.<P>Vertical depth = 8 inches<BR>Side to side width = 10 inches<BR>Front to back = 6 inches<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/battery3.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||03-25-2001||01:19 PM||||How did you run the positive cable? what did you use for a ground?<P>Thanks<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||03-25-2001||01:45 PM||||Again, I'm feeling very lazy today, first "do nothing" weekend in a while. Look up my topic where I chronicled this mod about this time last year. I explained the whole thing. I used welding cable that you can buy in bulk by the foot. Believe I used 2 gauge wire for the positive and 4 or 6 gauge for the negative. I ran a short ground to the frame up front and a long one to the engine (hence using thinner gauge wire since I had two grounds).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||mbramble||03-25-2001||02:00 PM||||Batboy,<P>Thanks much!!  That's just what I was looking for.  Sorry to get you off the couch.  I look forward to those lazy weekends myself.  Unfortunately since the weather has turned really nice here, I think my wife will keep me busy with honey-dos for quite awhile.....  But, at least she let me park the 'new' GT project car under the carport.  I really figured I'd be working on it in the yard!!<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
