Z||000014||mbramble||03-28-2001||09:53 AM||||Well, I am making my own out of fiberglass.  Using the dimensions provided above, I made up a 'mold' using posterboard and a couple of staples to hold it together.  I have laid about 3 layers of stranded fiberglass mesh over it and it has come out very nice.  I will probably add two more layers tonight.  I was concerned about ever peeling the posterboard out of the inside but it has been impregnated with resin and is now a very hard, smooth, paintable surface.  I had the resin and fiberglass laying around so, so far, it has cost me 'nothing'.  I will buy another package of the mesh tonight.  <P>Thanks much for the help.  I am looking foward to finishing it up and installing it over the weekend....<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||deceler8||03-28-2001||10:21 AM||||Once I had to make a battery box for another car and I discovered one of those boxes that hold six quarts of oil was the exact size I needed so I glassed the inside of the box and then soaked it in water to dissolve the cardboard.<P>Once the cardboard was gone I smoothed it out and painted it.<P>If you have one of these boxes lying around, give it a try. It might just work as a form.||||reg||1
Z||000016||FieroLT1||03-28-2001||12:06 PM||||To all this talk about the box size no one has addressed the battery size scenario. I think is important to point out that using the Fiero battery is a must or a replacement of the very same size. This is something that escaped me when I did my V8 swap, and since my fiero battery was dead anyways, I strolled down to Sears and got me an 850 cold cranking amps DieHard Gold. I was still ticked off by the fact that the 900 amps one was the same price but it wouldn't fit in the fiberglass box. The 850 amps fits just fine, BUT... now I can't fit the spare tire over it. Bummer! So, think about this for a while.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR> <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Will||03-28-2001||12:09 PM||||I'm having a local fab shop make me one out of stainless steel. I'm using different dimensions. My box will hold just about any car battery you can find. Does anyone want me to have one made for them? I haven't got the quote back yet, so I don't know exactly how much it will cost.||||reg||1
