Z||000023||85Josh||03-29-2001||05:35 PM||||Will, will the spare tire fit over your setup? I don't really care, but it is always nice to have a spare. If it really turns out to be $35, put me down for one.E-mail with details when you have them. Thanks, I appreciate the R&R!<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4<BR>CAVALRY SCOUT!(stuck in Field Artillery)||||reg||1
Z||000024||batboy||03-29-2001||07:58 PM||||When I was in the process of installing my box, I initially stuck a top post battery in it to take a couple pics and to see how the spare tire would fit. The steel rim of the spare touched the top posts of that battery and suddenly there was sparks, fireworks, and sizzling noise. Do not use a top post. Besides, you want the side posts sticking out the front so you can jump start the car without having to remove the spare each time. Here are some pics to help you guys visualize the project (these are not mine, I stole them from some website).<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.cwestco.com/Upgrades/Upgr_gif/Batbox1_500.GIF"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.cwestco.com/Upgrades/Upgr_gif/Batboxfr.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.cwestco.com/Upgrades/Upgr_gif/Batbxins.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000025||batboy||03-29-2001||08:18 PM||||Ok, I found my old topic thread from over a year ago tucked away back in the archives. How time flies when we're having fun.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-002567.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-002567.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||mbramble||03-29-2001||08:22 PM||||Well, I must have done something wrong when making up my box!!  I just don't see anyway that it's gonna clear that stabilizer bar up front that is right below the brake lines.  I haven't cut anything yet and it's hard to make accurate measurements to see where things are really going to fall into place but I just can't see not hitting that bar.  <P>The box I made is to the measurements given above.  Now there is no depth at the top of my box.  It's 6" in at the bottom and 0 at the top.  Looking at the West box, it looks like there is a little inset at the top which would change the angle at the back of the box but it still looks as though it would hit the bar.....<P>Any ideas on where I screwed up??  I don't have any photos but it looks exactly like the box in batboy's photo above except it is fiberglass and there is no inset in the top.  I don't have any problems making another, the biggest part is just waiting for the glass to dry.  I probably have two hours of actual working time in the thing and $12 worth of resin and cloth if I have to do it over again.  <P>Yea, batboy, I just found your old topic as well.<p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 03-29-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000027||Will||03-31-2001||03:22 AM||||I did some fairly careful measurements today, and gained a new respect for the design of the West Coast Fiero box. Someone put a good bit of time into getting that right. The part of the battery that sticks out is almost perfectly nested in the spare, and the part that protrudes through the plastic bulkhead is very close to sway bar.<P>The design of my box doesn't have a prayer of getting the spare in, but will hold a much larger battery.||||reg||1
Z||000028||mbramble||04-01-2001||12:38 PM||||Well....  Went ahead and cut the hole out in the front compartment figuring that if box didn't fit, I could take more measurements and modify/rebuild it so that it did.  It fits!!  Misses both the sway bar and the steering doodad (damper??).  Waiting for the paint on the box to dry and then I'll bolt it in.  Next -- running the new battery cables.<P>Thanks for all the help.  I had wanted to do this on my 87 for a long time but was a bit squeemish about it.  Since this 85 won't be on the road for awhile, I figured it couldn't hurt trying.  Total cost for the box -- $12 for fiberglass resin and cloth.<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
